This is more a design feature than a bug.  The answer to the question
"What to wish for" isn't the item that should have been wished for.
In Nethack and goal is information more than anything else.  What
to wish for is a list and/or strategy that lets you decide on the spot
when the wish happens.  Nethack works by game turn and a wish,
its prompt and getting the item all occur within a single game turn.

You can't save without wasting the wish, you have to have thought it
through in advance.  Absolutely standard Nethack design - Learn
by getting it wrong one or more times before you figure out a strategy
not a reaction.



